    LineComment "// A readable-member requirement. An interface member written `X: T` — no"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// parentheses — requires a member readable as `value.X` of type T, met by a field"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// or a getter, the two readable members. It is the requirement side of"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// read/projection symmetry: `X: T` is read (value.X), `X(): T` is called"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// (value.X()). Conformance is kind-aware — a field or getter meets `X: T`, a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// method meets `X(): T` — so a type opts into the behaviour by being readable the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// way the interface demands, with the read type checked against the requirement."
